&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fo60drcwvxvceaawcu631.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fo60drcwvxvceaawcu631.png" alt="AI Nature Explorer homepage showing the nature photo upload interface" width="800" height="362"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
What if technology could encourage us to spend more time outdoors instead of staying in front of a screen?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That idea inspired me to build &lt;strong&gt;AI Nature Explorer&lt;/strong&gt; 🌱&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


💡 What is it?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI Nature Explorer is a web application designed to help people explore nature. Users can upload a photo of a plant, flower, tree, or another part of nature, with the goal of identifying the image and receiving an outdoor mission.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fv2auyg2swl5iv896rge0.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fv2auyg2swl5iv896rge0.png" alt="AI Nature Explorer displaying a nature image classification result" width="597" height="623"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


🛠️ Tech Stack
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FastAPI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hugging Face Transformers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vercel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Render&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


🌍 What I learned
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building this project helped me practise frontend and backend integration, connect a React application to a Python API, deploy a frontend, and troubleshoot deployment and memory-limit issues.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fsewc22do4ngsogk3m103.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fsewc22do4ngsogk3m103.png" alt="AI Nature Explorer showing an outdoor nature exploration mission" width="800" height="449"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The AI backend still needs deployment improvements, so the live identification feature is a work in progress.&lt;/p&gt;

